Diaphora
========

DSigMatcher's diff engine is a C++ port of the diffing logic of Diaphora:

    Diaphora, a binary diffing tool
    Copyright (c) 2015-2026 Joxean Koret
    Licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 or
    (at your option) any later version.
    https://github.com/joxeankoret/diaphora

Ported revision: 3.4.2-4-g621ec26
(commit 621ec2699255fa709b2ee422cd919b38f088f16b).

What was taken from Diaphora and how it was modified (AGPL-3.0 section 5(a)).
The work was done in September 2026, for the v1.0.0 release.

  * The diff engine (src/diff/ and include/dsigmatcher/diff/) translates
    Diaphora's CBinDiff.diff() pipeline from Python into C++20: the match
    bookkeeping, the ratio computation, the pre-loop passes, the heuristic
    tiers, callee diffing, related constants, related compilation units, local
    affinity, the final multimatch pass and the writer of the .diaphora
    results file. Comments of the form "D:<line>" cite the diaphora.py line
    each piece of code was translated from.
  * src/diff/RegistrySql.inc and src/diff/StageSql.inc embed Diaphora's SQL
    verbatim: the 50 heuristic queries of diaphora_heuristics.py and the stage
    queries of diaphora.py. They are generated from an unmodified Diaphora
    checkout by tools/parity/gen_registry.py.
  * The result-porting command (src/cli/PortResults.cpp) reads Diaphora's
    results-file layout.
  * The design documents under docs/parity/ quote Diaphora's source code.

Diaphora itself is not included in the source tree or in any release
archive. The extract, ingest and update commands run an unmodified Diaphora
checkout that the user supplies (see README.md).


